✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿
✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿
§5 ⚜ ᴀ ꜱᴛᴏʀʏ ꜱᴇʀɪᴇꜱ ⚜
#- §5╔═.✵.════════╗  §2      ʀᴇᴅᴇᴍᴘᴛɪᴏɴ
§5╚════════.✵.═╝
§2The glitched world around them twisted and contorted, bending to the will of some unseen force. The sky was an inky black, dotted with stars that seemed to pulse with an eerie light. The ground was rough and uneven,§r
#- §2littered with strange, gnarled trees and vines that seemed to writhe and twist in the shadows. Fern and Castien were immediately struck by the oppressive sense of dread that hung over the place. The air was thick with the stench of decay. They knew they were in danger, but had no§r  
#- §2idea how to escape.

As they ventured deeper into the glitch dimension, they encountered strange misshapen creatures, their limbs elongated and their eyes glowing with an otherworldly light. Despite their fear, Fern and Castien pressed on. But the deeper they§r 
#- §2ventured, the more they realised that they were hopelessly lost. 

And then they heard it. A low, guttural growl that echoed all around them. Fern collapsed on the ground, gasping for air. Withering. Castien was quick to react and picked her§r
#- §2up in his arms. They searched for an exit, but every path led them back to where they started. Time worked differently here. In fact, almost everything did. With no hunger or thirst or need of sleep, days turned into weeks, weeks turned into months, and months turned into years.§r
#- §2As time passed, they began to rely on each other. They shared their fears, hopes, and dreams. One night, as they sat by the dim glow of a dying fire, Fern confessed her feelings for Castien. She had never felt this way about anyone before. Castien was surprised, but he couldn't deny the way§r
#- §2his heart raced at the thought of Fern. As they shared their first kiss, it felt like they were the only two people in the world. And they were. 

They knew they may never escape this dimension, but they didn't care. They had each other, and that was enough.§r
#- §2But as their love grew stronger, so did the horror of their situation. The glitches in the dimension became more frequent and terrifying. They would see shadowy figures lurking, hear whispers that sounded like they were right next to them, a cold breath on their necks when they were alone.§r
#- §2They began to see things, things that shouldn't exist. They didn’t know what was real anymore...§r

§6Somewhere in a time and space far from this glitched nightmare, a Witch found herself in the confines of Link's Laboratory. Grappling with the aftermath of§r
#- §6a harrowing ordeal.

The Witch got out of bed, her lavender hair floating wildly around her. She stood tall, with emerald eyes blazing. She closed her eyes, feeling the pulsing energy within her surge, as she summoned magic, that deep down, she didn't have to spare.§r
#- §6Her graceful but shaking fingers curled into a tight fist, and she chanted ancient incantations that echoed through the air, drawing upon the forces of the universe. Her soul traveled far back in time, her spirit soaring through the many realms of the past, guided by her faith.§r
#- §6With every beat of her heart, she could feel the weight of her mistakes and regrets, and with every breath, she harnessed the wish of redemption. 

Her power crackled and surged through the laboratory as she rewrote the threads of time, weaving them into a new tapestry.§r
#- §6As she opened her eyes, she found herself standing in the midst of the past, ready to right her wrongs and rewrite the story. She called out into the vast darkness....§r

§2One night, as Fern & Castien lay together, they heard a sound. It was a soft whisper,§r
#- §2barely audible. They listened closely, and they could hear a voice calling their names. They thought it was their imagination, but the voice grew louder. Suddenly, the air around them glitched and flickered  and the darkness was replaced by blinding light. They shielded their eyes and§r
#- §2looked up to see a figure standing before them. It was a humanoid figure, but it's face was distorted and glitched. The figure reached out a hand, and it’s glitches began to fade away.  The figure became clearer. It was a person, a familiar person Fern met a very long time ago§r
#- §2in the snow. The pale pink toned skin with bright green eyes, a dress of flowers and leaves floating as though they were underwater, sparks of magical energy surrounding them. 
It was The Witch, Sweetpea! She calmly explained how she had come back to save them, and that she§r  
#- §2refused to let the story end like this.

Fern and Castien were concerned yet overjoyed. They could finally be together in the real world. They took each other's hand and followed the light.  Leaving behind the dimension that should never have been!§r
#- §2To be continued…
§5✿✿❀❀❀✿✿.✿✿❀❀❀✿✿

